WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.690
My name is Nanfu.

00:00:15.365 --> 00:00:18.240
In Chinese, "nan" means "man."

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:20.769
And "fu" means "pillar."

00:00:21.579 --> 00:00:23.692
My family had hoped for a boy,

00:00:23.716 --> 00:00:27.049
who would grow up
to be the pillar of the family.

00:00:27.692 --> 00:00:29.931
And when I turned out to be a girl,

00:00:29.955 --> 00:00:31.811
they named me Nanfu anyway.

00:00:31.835 --> 00:00:33.260
(Laughter)

00:00:33.284 --> 00:00:35.712
I was born in 1985,

00:00:35.736 --> 00:00:39.403
six years before China announced
its one-child policy.

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:43.204
Right after I was born,

00:00:43.228 --> 00:00:47.283
the local officials came
and ordered my mom to be sterilized.

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:51.100
My grandpa stood up to the officials,

00:00:51.124 --> 00:00:54.510
because he wanted a grandson
to carry on the family name.

00:00:55.982 --> 00:01:00.153
Eventually, my parents were allowed
to have a second child,

00:01:00.177 --> 00:01:02.249
but they had to wait for five years

00:01:02.273 --> 00:01:04.073
and pay a substantial fine.

00:01:05.638 --> 00:01:08.535
Growing up, my brother and I

00:01:08.559 --> 00:01:11.687
were surrounded by children
from one-child families.

00:01:13.004 --> 00:01:16.042
I remember feeling a sense of shame

00:01:16.066 --> 00:01:17.821
because I had a younger brother.

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:22.725
I felt like our family did something wrong
for having two children.

00:01:24.315 --> 00:01:25.800
At the time, I didn't question

00:01:25.824 --> 00:01:28.662
where this sense of shame
and guilt came from.

00:01:31.062 --> 00:01:34.356
A year and a half ago,
I had my own first child.

00:01:34.991 --> 00:01:37.919
It was the best thing
that ever happened in my life.

00:01:38.538 --> 00:01:39.839
Becoming a mother

00:01:39.863 --> 00:01:43.942
gave me a totally new perspective
on my own childhood,

00:01:43.966 --> 00:01:48.466
and it brought back
my memories of early life in China.

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:51.617
For the past three decades,

00:01:51.641 --> 00:01:56.363
everyone in my family had to apply
for a permission from the government

00:01:56.387 --> 00:01:57.537
to have a child.

00:01:58.369 --> 00:01:59.718
And I wondered

00:01:59.742 --> 00:02:03.938
what it was like for people
who lived under the one-child policy.

00:02:04.361 --> 00:02:07.361
So I decided to make
a documentary about it.

00:02:08.964 --> 00:02:10.869
One of the people I interviewed

00:02:10.893 --> 00:02:16.051
was the midwife who delivered
all of the babies born in my village,

00:02:16.075 --> 00:02:17.225
including myself.

00:02:18.456 --> 00:02:21.620
She was 84 years old
when I interviewed her.

00:02:22.294 --> 00:02:24.018
I asked her,

00:02:24.042 --> 00:02:27.708
"Do you remember how many babies
you delivered throughout your career?"

00:02:28.399 --> 00:02:30.633
She didn't have a number for deliveries.

00:02:31.561 --> 00:02:34.812
She said she had performed

00:02:34.836 --> 00:02:39.411
60,000 forced abortions
and sterilizations.

00:02:40.855 --> 00:02:43.165
Sometimes, she said,

00:02:43.189 --> 00:02:46.276
a late-term fetus
would survive an abortion,

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.009
and she would kill the baby
after delivering it.

00:02:49.489 --> 00:02:53.220
She remembered how her hands would tremble

00:02:53.244 --> 00:02:54.577
as she did the work.

00:02:55.815 --> 00:02:57.215
Her story shocked me.

00:02:57.934 --> 00:03:00.141
When I set out to make the film,

00:03:00.165 --> 00:03:04.582
I expected it would be a simple story
of perpetrators and victims.

00:03:04.606 --> 00:03:06.534
People who carried out the policy

00:03:06.558 --> 00:03:09.142
and people who are living
with the consequences.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:11.501
But that wasn't what I saw.

00:03:12.082 --> 00:03:15.286
As I was finishing
my interview with the midwife,

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:17.541
I noticed an area in her house

00:03:17.565 --> 00:03:21.833
that was decorated
with elaborate homemade flags.

00:03:21.857 --> 00:03:24.927
And each flag has a picture
of a baby on it.

00:03:26.157 --> 00:03:29.299
These were flags
that were sent by families

00:03:29.323 --> 00:03:33.204
whom she helped treat
their infertility problems.

00:03:33.657 --> 00:03:35.990
She explained that she had had enough

00:03:36.014 --> 00:03:38.950
of performing abortions
and sterilizations --

00:03:38.974 --> 00:03:43.590
that the only work she did now
was to help families have babies.

00:03:44.839 --> 00:03:47.283
She said she was full of guilt

00:03:47.307 --> 00:03:50.202
for carrying out the one-child policy,

00:03:50.226 --> 00:03:53.470
and she hoped that by helping
families have babies,

00:03:53.494 --> 00:03:56.470
she could counteract
what she did in the past.

00:03:57.034 --> 00:04:01.830
It became clear to me
she, too, was a victim of the policy.

00:04:02.973 --> 00:04:05.664
Every voice was telling her

00:04:05.688 --> 00:04:09.155
that what she did was right
and necessary for China's survival.

00:04:10.108 --> 00:04:13.042
And she did what she thought
was right for her country.

00:04:14.265 --> 00:04:16.733
I know how strong that message was.

00:04:17.273 --> 00:04:20.281
It was everywhere
around myself when I grew up.

00:04:20.305 --> 00:04:23.029
It was printed on matches,

00:04:23.053 --> 00:04:24.689
playing cards,

00:04:24.713 --> 00:04:26.775
textbooks, posters.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.243
The propaganda praising
the one-child policy

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:30.949
was everywhere around us.

00:04:30.973 --> 00:04:33.521
[Anyone who refuses to sterilize
will be arrested.]

00:04:33.545 --> 00:04:35.879
And so were the threats
against disobeying it.

00:04:35.903 --> 00:04:38.339
The message seeped into our minds

00:04:38.363 --> 00:04:41.568
so much so that I grew up
feeling embarrassed

00:04:41.592 --> 00:04:43.380
for having a younger brother.

00:04:45.625 --> 00:04:48.459
With each person I filmed,

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:55.890
I saw how their minds and hearts
can be influenced by the propaganda,

00:04:55.914 --> 00:05:00.009
and how their willingness
to make sacrifices for the greater good

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:03.500
can be twisted into something
very dark and tragic.

00:05:04.466 --> 00:05:08.418
China is not the only place
where this happens.

00:05:08.442 --> 00:05:13.632
There is no country on earth
where propaganda isn't present.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:18.815
And in societies that are supposed to be
more open and free than China,

00:05:18.839 --> 00:05:22.999
it can be even harder to recognize
what propaganda looks like.

00:05:23.728 --> 00:05:27.363
It hides in plain sight as news reports,

00:05:27.387 --> 00:05:31.424
TV commercials, political campaigning

00:05:31.448 --> 00:05:33.254
and in our social media feeds.

00:05:34.347 --> 00:05:38.132
It works to change our minds
without our knowledge.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:45.403
Every society is vulnerable
to accepting propaganda as truth,

00:05:45.427 --> 00:05:48.235
and no society where propaganda
replaces the truth

00:05:48.259 --> 00:05:50.021
can be truly free.

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:51.507
Thank you.

00:05:51.531 --> 00:05:55.547
(Applause)

